.TH BLKCP 1 "September 2026" "blkcp (High-Performance Block Copy Utility)" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
blkcp \- high-performance block copy utility with dynamic autotuning, io_uring, zero-copy reflink, streaming hash and safety guards
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B blkcp
[\fI\,OPTIONS\/\fR] [\fI\,INPUT\/\fR] [\fI\,OUTPUT\/\fR]
.br
.B blkcp
\fB-i\fR \fI\,INPUT\/\fR \fB-o\fR \fI\,OUTPUT\/\fR [\fI\,OPTIONS\/\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBblkcp\fR is a modern, ultra-high-performance block replication and stream imaging tool designed from the ground up to replace traditional dd.
.PP
Key capabilities include asynchronous \fBio_uring\fR kernel streaming, multi-threaded ringbuffer double-buffering, Linux kernel zero-copy reflink cloning via \fBcopy_file_range(2)\fR, real-time dynamic I/O autotuning, hardware block-size awareness, streaming cryptographic SHA-256 integrity verification, and an active Target Safety Guard preventing catastrophic accidental host filesystem destruction.

.SH CORE OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-input\fR=\fI\,FILE\/\fR
Specify the input file, block device or stream (default: standard input).
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR=\fI\,FILE\/\fR
Specify the output destination file, block device or stream (default: standard output).
.TP
\fB\-b\fR, \fB\-\-block\-size\fR=\fI\,SIZE\/\fR
Uniform block transfer size (e.g. \fB64K\fR, \fB1M\fR, \fB4M\fR, \fB16M\fR). Passing \fBauto\fR enables dynamic in-flight autotuning.
.TP
\fB\-e\fR, \fB\-\-engine\fR=\fI\,ENGINE\/\fR
Select the low-level data transfer execution engine:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
\fBuring\fR: Linux \fBio_uring\fR kernel submission/completion ring pipeline. Delivers maximum async throughput with minimal syscall overhead.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBasync\fR: Multi-threaded pthread double-buffering pipeline with isolated background reader/writer ringbuffers.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBreflink\fR: Zero-copy in-kernel cloning via \fBcopy_file_range(2)\fR (instantaneous on CoW filesystems like Btrfs/XFS/ZFS).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBsplice\fR: Zero-copy in-kernel pipe and stream pipeline via \fBsplice(2)\fR.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBsync\fR: Direct synchronous block I/O with optional dynamic autotuning.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBauto\fR: Intelligent auto-detection (opportunistic reflink -> io_uring/async -> sync).
.RE
.TP
\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-limit\fR=\fI\,BYTES\/\fR, \fB\-\-size\fR=\fI\,BYTES\/\fR
Exact transfer byte limit regardless of block alignment.
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-count\fR=\fI\,N\/\fR
Copy only \fIN\fR input blocks.
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-progress\fR
Display live real-time transfer telemetry and transfer speeds on stderr.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit machine-readable NDJSON telemetry lines on stderr (\fBevent: progress\fR and \fBevent: finished\fR).
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress all output except fatal error messages.
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-force\fR
Override the Target Safety Guard when attempting to write to devices hosting mounted root/boot partitions.
.TP
\fB\-\-hash\fR, \fB\-\-sha256\fR
Compute on-the-fly streaming SHA-256 cryptographic digest without requiring an extra I/O pass.
.TP
\fB\-\-autotune\fR
Benchmark and dynamically scale the block size during the initial transfer phase for peak bus throughput.
.TP
\fB\-\-direct\fR
Enable direct I/O (\fBO_DIRECT\fR) bypassing the kernel page cache.
.TP
\fB\-\-nocache\fR
Discard operating system page cache in 32-MiB streaming intervals via posix_fadvise(POSIX_FADV_DONTNEED).
.TP
\fB\-\-queue\-depth\fR=\fI\,N\/\fR, \fB\-\-async\-queue\fR=\fI\,N\/\fR
Set the multi-threaded ringbuffer slot capacity for the \fBasync\fR engine (between 2 and 1024 slots). Defaults to dynamic adaptive scaling (auto) based on block size and target buffer budget.
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\fR=\fI\,BYTES\/\fR
Skip \fIBYTES\fR at input before copying.
.TP
\fB\-\-seek\fR=\fI\,BYTES\/\fR
Seek \fIBYTES\fR at output before writing.
.TP
\fB\-\-sparse\fR
Punch holes or create sparse files for zero-filled blocks.
.TP
\fB\-\-sync\fR
Pad short reads with zero bytes up to block size.
.TP
\fB\-\-notrunc\fR
Do not truncate the target output file.
.TP
\fB\-\-noerror\fR
Continue copying across bad sectors or read errors.
.TP
\fB\-\-fdatasync\fR
Synchronously flush output data before exiting.
.TP
\fB\-\-fsync\fR
Synchronously flush output data and metadata before exiting.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Display comprehensive help manual and exit.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Display version information and exit.

.SH TARGET SAFETY GUARD
\fBblkcp\fR inspects target block devices prior to opening. If the target device holds an active system mount (e.g. \fB/\fR, \fB/boot\fR, \fB/usr\fR, \fB/home\fR) or is an active system swap partition, write execution is immediately refused unless \fB-f\fR or \fB--force\fR is explicitly supplied.

.SH SIGNAL HANDLING
Sending \fBSIGUSR1\fR to a running \fBblkcp\fR process causes it to output current I/O progress and speed statistics to standard error before resuming operation.

.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Clone a raw disk image with io_uring and live progress telemetry:
.RS
.B blkcp -i /dev/nvme0n1 -o backup.raw -b 4M -e uring -p
.RE
.PP
Instantaneous zero-copy reflink duplicate:
.RS
.B blkcp -i source.iso -o clone.iso -e reflink -p
.RE
.PP
Copy exact 10 GB limit with streaming SHA-256 verification:
.RS
.B blkcp -i /dev/urandom -o test.img -l 10G -e uring --hash
.RE

